WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.100
So a fire breaks out.

2
00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:04.775
What do you do, and in what order?

3
00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:11.600
First, raise the alarm, get life jackets on everyone, and move your passengers away from the fire.

4
00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.525
People first.

5
00:00:13.775 --> 00:00:15.700
Second, use the boat.

6
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:20.500
Turn so the wind carries the smoke and flames away from your people.

7
00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.800
Usually that means putting the fire downwind.

8
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:28.325
Third, the extinguisher, and here’s the word to remember: PASS.

9
00:00:28.575 --> 00:00:30.200
Pull the pin.

10
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.575
Aim at the base of the fire.

11
00:00:32.825 --> 00:00:34.575
Squeeze the handle.

12
00:00:34.825 --> 00:00:36.925
Sweep from side to side.

13
00:00:37.175 --> 00:00:38.775
Why the base?

14
00:00:39.775 --> 00:00:42.050
Because that’s where the fuel is.

15
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.650
Spraying the flames does nothing.

16
00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.125
Keep an escape route behind you.

17
00:00:47.375 --> 00:00:50.675
Never let the fire get between you and the way out.

18
00:00:50.925 --> 00:00:52.800
And know when to quit.

19
00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.600
A small boat fire grows fast.

20
00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:00.225
If it isn’t out in seconds, call Mayday and prepare to abandon.
